Please tell us what's going on.

00:00:56.286 --> 00:00:57.162
NANO POWER BUTANE GAS

00:00:57.245 --> 00:00:58.497
Was it really a butane gas explosion?

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:00.624
Was it really butane gas?

00:01:02.042 --> 00:01:04.169
Why the sudden rush
with the investigation?

00:01:04.252 --> 00:01:05.462
Please say something!

00:01:06.254 --> 00:01:07.214
Please!

00:01:07.589 --> 00:01:09.925
If it led to some hair burning
or a dining table blowing up,

00:01:10.258 --> 00:01:11.510
then it would've made sense.

00:01:11.593 --> 00:01:12.552
NANO POWER BUTANE GAS RESEARCHER

00:01:12.636 --> 00:01:15.305
But butane gas blowing up
a whole ATM booth?

00:01:16.014 --> 00:01:17.641
You've got to be kidding me.

00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:21.478
Why would North Korea even need to bother
experimenting with missiles, then?

00:01:21.687 --> 00:01:22.979
They should just use our butane gas!

00:01:23.063 --> 00:01:26.566
HARDWARE DREAM TREE STATIONERY
When this blew up,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.819
I was standing right here.

00:01:28.902 --> 00:01:32.322
The only reason I survived
was because I ducked so quickly.

00:01:32.656 --> 00:01:35.283
If I were even slightly slower,
I could've died.

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.911
MAMMOSEU MART DELIVERY MAN
Someone died in the ATM booth overnight,

00:01:37.994 --> 00:01:42.165
yet new ATM machines were set up
by the next morning.

00:01:42.249 --> 00:01:45.377
Is anyone really that rushed for cash?
Somebody just died.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.878
That's wrong.

00:01:47.045 --> 00:01:49.673
Just a few days after the ATM explosion,

00:01:49.756 --> 00:01:52.134
another explosion took place in Kiyun-si.

00:01:52.843 --> 00:01:56.388
At the bus terminal behind me,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.183
a bus exploded, killing two civilians.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:05.105
So why hasn't the government
announced anything yet?

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.857
BUS DRIVER OF THE EXPLODED BUS
It just exploded.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.651
The bus wasn't even burning
or smoking beforehand.

00:02:09.735 --> 00:02:11.027
It just blew up.

00:02:11.111 --> 00:02:11.945
MAMMOSEU MART OWNER

00:02:12.028 --> 00:02:13.363
It was around 7 a.m.

00:02:13.447 --> 00:02:14.865
- It's Mom.
- It's your mom.

00:02:14.948 --> 00:02:15.782
- Quiet.
- It's Mom.

00:02:15.866 --> 00:02:17.159
She looks nice and scary.

00:02:17.576 --> 00:02:20.162
The commander's lead car
was at the bus terminal.

00:02:20.579 --> 00:02:23.999
Are you sure you saw it?
And how did you know?

00:02:24.916 --> 00:02:26.668
Well, it was a Retona.

00:02:26.918 --> 00:02:30.756
Anyway, the traffic was so bad
that my car was barely moving.

00:02:31.256 --> 00:02:34.426
But the police and the firefighters
were just standing guard

00:02:34.593 --> 00:02:36.386
while soldiers were cleaning up the site.

00:02:36.803 --> 00:02:39.598
We send our sons to the military
to protect the nation,

00:02:39.681 --> 00:02:41.850
not to clean up some random neighborhood.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:45.228
If they were there for civilian support,
they should've helped the people.

00:02:46.563 --> 00:02:48.148
MAGNIFYING MEDIA
Experts and witnesses

00:02:48.231 --> 00:02:50.817
suspect these explosions
to have been bombs instead of butane gas.

00:02:51.651 --> 00:02:53.570
The soldiers at the site.

00:02:53.653 --> 00:02:57.032
Most importantly, the government seems
too eager to rush to close this case.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.994
The series of explosions in Kiyun-si
is full of questions.

00:03:01.661 --> 00:03:03.371
What is true,

00:03:04.039 --> 00:03:06.416
and what is the government hiding?

00:03:09.461 --> 00:03:14.049
EPISODE 4: WHAT BRINGS YOU TO OUR TOWN?

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:19.888
Did you watch the clip?

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:22.432
Who uploaded that?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.062
You idiot. I told you
to stop these clips from circulating!

00:03:29.523 --> 00:03:30.732
Forget it.

00:03:32.275 --> 00:03:36.488
Don't let anyone approach Kiyun-si
until we find out what's going on.

00:03:45.872 --> 00:03:48.166
It wasn't the 88th Transportation Brigade?

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.462
What about the 900th Unit
or the Logistic Support Group?

00:03:54.965 --> 00:03:58.593
What do you mean, "standby squad"?

00:03:58.677 --> 00:04:00.720
There are witnesses
who saw military vehicles.

00:04:00.804 --> 00:04:03.431
And you're seriously saying
no military units were deployed?

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:05.267
Keep searching.

00:04:09.896 --> 00:04:11.857
These bastards are messing with me.

00:04:12.399 --> 00:04:14.234
Maybe they really don't know
what's going on, either.

00:04:15.026 --> 00:04:16.236
That's an even bigger issue.

00:04:22.284 --> 00:04:24.703
Look into what those four talked about.

00:04:24.953 --> 00:04:28.582
It seems to have something to do
with the explosions in Kiyun-si.

00:04:29.207 --> 00:04:30.208
Yes, sir.

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:33.295
- This is just between us.
- Understood, sir.

00:05:01.239 --> 00:05:04.242
OPERATION JINDO DOG
TOP SECRET MILITARY SECURITY

00:05:08.788 --> 00:05:12.667
CHOI KANG

00:05:15.128 --> 00:05:16.963
RECENT MISSION:
HOSTAGE RESCUE IN NORTHERN IRAQ

00:05:17.047 --> 00:05:20.216
RESIDENCE: KIYUN-SI, GANGWON-DO

00:05:26.181 --> 00:05:28.183
So in summary,

00:05:28.642 --> 00:05:31.144
you were checking if he was a spy
or from the National Intelligence Service.

00:05:31.227 --> 00:05:34.522
Then you saw those stuffed bunnies
and found this laptop?

00:05:34.606 --> 00:05:35.440
Yes.

00:05:35.523 --> 00:05:39.027
And the man who died in the ATM explosion
and the man from the building are a team.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.613
And you're saying
the bus terminal explosion is related too?

00:05:41.696 --> 00:05:43.990
Yes, this is the stuffed bunny.

00:05:44.282 --> 00:05:48.244
That was a great summary.
No wonder you're a journalist.

00:05:48.536 --> 00:05:51.831
But how did you take down
that armed agent?

00:05:52.832 --> 00:05:53.708
Well...

00:05:56.211 --> 00:05:58.421
I can throw some spicy punches!

00:05:59.214 --> 00:06:01.091
SPECIAL MARTIAL ARTS

00:06:01.675 --> 00:06:03.718
I also served in the HID.

00:06:03.802 --> 00:06:05.220
You know that unit, right?

00:06:05.303 --> 00:06:06.471
You know, from that movie.

00:06:09.349 --> 00:06:10.976
"I'll rip out your gold teeth

00:06:12.018 --> 00:06:13.853
and tear you apart."

00:06:23.989 --> 00:06:25.949
And I can run really fast.

00:06:26.658 --> 00:06:29.369
So we fought that guy

00:06:29.452 --> 00:06:31.121
while he ran off.

00:06:31.204 --> 00:06:32.539
That's right!

00:06:33.164 --> 00:06:37.168
So why are you telling me all this?

00:06:38.253 --> 00:06:42.549
I want to uncover the truth
behind Myeong-o's death.

00:06:43.383 --> 00:06:46.886
People in our neighborhood are dying.
We need to do something.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.221
Same here.

00:06:48.304 --> 00:06:52.517
I wonder if I caused all this trouble
by stealing this laptop.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.436
Hey, how is that your fault?

00:07:10.952 --> 00:07:12.412
THEY'RE LISTENING, SHUSH

00:07:12.871 --> 00:07:13.997
But the power is off--

00:07:14.622 --> 00:07:15.832
It's off, though.

00:07:21.379 --> 00:07:22.422
THAT LAPTOP CAN STILL LISTEN IN

00:07:24.674 --> 00:07:25.800
EVEN WHEN IT'S OFF

00:07:27.761 --> 00:07:28.970
IF THEY CAN TAP US,
THEY CAN TRACK OUR LOCATION

00:07:42.233 --> 00:07:44.486
WHAT IF WE USE IT AGAINST THEM?

00:07:52.744 --> 00:07:56.414
We need to clone the original laptop!

00:07:56.498 --> 00:07:59.501
- We pull the data with forensics...
- And secure evidence!

00:07:59.584 --> 00:08:02.295
And since they can track our location
using the laptop...

00:08:02.378 --> 00:08:05.048
- We'll purposely expose our location...
- To catch the culprit!

00:08:10.053 --> 00:08:14.015
Then we need to start
with the CMOS battery first!

00:08:14.099 --> 00:08:16.851
Hey, I can take care of that!

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.521
Okay, that's all for today! Dismissed!

00:08:19.979 --> 00:08:22.190
Hold up! What are you going to do?

00:08:22.482 --> 00:08:25.485
Go to work! I have a job!

00:08:26.569 --> 00:08:27.654
Okay, dismissed!

00:08:31.908 --> 00:08:34.786
My goodness, that's intense.

00:08:34.869 --> 00:08:36.162
That's his car.

00:08:36.246 --> 00:08:38.414
- Amazing.
- Will you look at that?

00:08:38.498 --> 00:08:40.500
Your car is incredible!

00:08:41.709 --> 00:08:43.044
That's neat.

00:08:43.128 --> 00:08:44.546
Can I get a ride?

00:08:47.757 --> 00:08:49.968
Why are they all coming out of there?

00:08:50.677 --> 00:08:51.803
Without me?

00:08:54.556 --> 00:08:56.057
INTERNET SECURITY TECHNOLOGY

00:08:56.141 --> 00:08:58.143
COMPUTER FORENSIC ANALYSIS

00:09:01.813 --> 00:09:04.566
It's going to take forever
on this computer.

00:09:32.343 --> 00:09:37.015
Since chip bags are made of
polypropylene and aluminum,

00:09:37.307 --> 00:09:39.017
they can block out electric signals,

00:09:40.643 --> 00:09:42.812
magnetic field signals,
and even telecommunication signals.

00:09:42.896 --> 00:09:45.398
See how dangerous the packaging is?

00:09:45.481 --> 00:09:47.775
This is why moms don't let kids eat chips.

00:09:48.151 --> 00:09:50.570
Chips are delicious, but dangerous.

00:09:50.653 --> 00:09:53.615
- That has nothing to do--
- Of course not.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:54.824
It's just a joke.

00:10:06.544 --> 00:10:08.963
- Officer Park! Someone is dying!
- What?

00:10:09.047 --> 00:10:11.507
- Someone's dying!
- Where?

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:13.259
Me.

00:10:13.343 --> 00:10:15.053
I'm so low on sugar
that I feel like dying.

00:10:15.345 --> 00:10:17.388
Man, you scared me!

00:10:17.472 --> 00:10:18.973
Buy me a cup of coffee.

00:10:23.645 --> 00:10:27.357
There are cafes all around,
yet you come to the police station?

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:30.526
Hey, you can't get
vending machine coffee at cafes.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:32.237
I love these.

00:10:36.032 --> 00:10:37.784
By the way,

00:10:38.493 --> 00:10:41.120
you know the foreigner
who lived in the apartment?

00:10:41.204 --> 00:10:43.998
I took something from Unit 203
of that building.

00:10:44.415 --> 00:10:48.836
It looks sketchy and dangerous,
so I'd like to leave it with the police.

00:10:49.212 --> 00:10:50.505
Why would you take anything?

00:10:50.588 --> 00:10:52.757
I didn't know it'd be so dangerous.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.259
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:10:54.342 --> 00:10:56.344
I'm turning myself in, okay?

00:10:56.427 --> 00:10:57.929
Cut me some slack.

00:11:08.106 --> 00:11:11.317
MAGNIFYING MEDIA

00:11:17.573 --> 00:11:19.492
I think we need to take it to a shop.

00:11:19.575 --> 00:11:22.078
I could do it, but I don't have the tools.

00:11:22.161 --> 00:11:23.079
How much would it be?

00:11:23.496 --> 00:11:25.957
For data extraction, memory analysis,

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.543
and reverse engineering, it'll be--

00:11:28.626 --> 00:11:31.170
So, how much will it be in total?

00:11:31.462 --> 00:11:33.256
About 20,000,000 won?

00:11:33.506 --> 00:11:34.340
Did you say 2,000 won?

00:11:34.424 --> 00:11:36.217
- You don't mean 20,000,000 won, right?
- What?

00:11:36.759 --> 00:11:38.636
For this?

00:11:39.804 --> 00:11:40.638
Yes.

00:11:41.222 --> 00:11:44.517
Man, that's too expensive.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:48.146
If the five of us were to split it...
No, leave the college student out.

00:11:48.229 --> 00:11:50.023
So, 5,000,000 won per person?

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.483
We can pay in installments.

00:11:52.567 --> 00:11:54.777
Yes, over 120 months.

00:11:54.861 --> 00:11:57.488
- Yes, do that.
- We should look for some other ways.

00:11:57.739 --> 00:11:58.865
I got it.

00:11:58.948 --> 00:11:59.991
- You did?
- What?

00:12:00.074 --> 00:12:02.368
With what money? You're a student.
What's the installment plan?

00:12:02.452 --> 00:12:04.245
I paid for everything at once.
With my mom's card.

00:12:05.538 --> 00:12:07.206
- No way!
- You're rich!

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:09.083
Don't you need to ask your mom first?

00:12:09.167 --> 00:12:10.543
Is your mom okay with it?

00:12:11.461 --> 00:12:12.712
- No way.
- Man...

00:12:12.795 --> 00:12:17.050
Now that we've got the tools,
I'll keep researching until they arrive.

00:12:17.175 --> 00:12:19.052
- I'll prepare the follow-up article.
- Okay.

00:12:19.135 --> 00:12:21.429
The computer signal disconnected
at the police station,

00:12:21.512 --> 00:12:22.889
so these guys will go there.

00:12:22.972 --> 00:12:26.684
Let's hide out at the station, then.

00:12:27.518 --> 00:12:29.145
You can join us at night after work.

00:12:29.562 --> 00:12:31.564
I can't do tomorrow.
I have a housewarming party.

00:12:31.647 --> 00:12:32.607
Really?

00:12:33.107 --> 00:12:35.485
Who will guard the station
if we're all there?

00:12:37.403 --> 00:12:38.321
All where?

00:12:38.529 --> 00:12:39.614
Your housewarming party.

00:12:39.697 --> 00:12:41.282
Aren't we all invited?

00:12:42.367 --> 00:12:43.785
I'm fine.

00:12:44.494 --> 00:12:46.621
I should attend as Do-yeon's master.

00:12:48.623 --> 00:12:49.916
Have you all lost your minds?

00:12:50.375 --> 00:12:51.876
I invited my colleagues from work!

00:12:53.002 --> 00:12:54.629
I wasn't going to go, anyway.

00:12:56.547 --> 00:12:58.633
My gosh!

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.637
Why did you even mention the party, then?

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.681
So, you only like your colleagues
and not your neighbors?

00:13:05.765 --> 00:13:07.225
Who's going to hide out, then?

00:13:07.725 --> 00:13:09.894
We can install a camera
at the station and record it.

00:13:10.603 --> 00:13:13.022
The data fee will be so high

00:13:13.481 --> 00:13:15.400
without the wi-fi feature
on the memory card, though.

00:13:15.483 --> 00:13:17.485
What? How much is that?

00:13:17.568 --> 00:13:19.987
I ordered the memory card
with the highest capacity.

00:13:20.071 --> 00:13:22.698
My gosh, what are you doing?

00:13:22.782 --> 00:13:26.244
We can't have you here
if you do that again!

00:13:26.327 --> 00:13:27.662
Hey, boss! You can be my boss now.

00:13:28.037 --> 00:13:30.373
- Yes.
- He's the boss.

00:13:30.456 --> 00:13:33.251
- Thank you.
- Yeah, thank you.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.974
What the hell?

00:15:55.184 --> 00:15:57.812
You scared me to death!

00:15:58.271 --> 00:15:59.981
Is that a security camera in your car?

00:16:00.189 --> 00:16:01.190
What?

00:16:01.816 --> 00:16:04.819
Oh, this? It's a custom-made dash cam.

00:16:05.194 --> 00:16:08.864
The data is sent to the cloud memory.

00:16:09.115 --> 00:16:10.700
If someone leaves a dent in my car,

00:16:10.783 --> 00:16:14.579
this will immediately send me a text.

00:16:15.663 --> 00:16:16.872
Text, my ass.

00:16:17.164 --> 00:16:20.209
Yong-hui's phone is off,
and look at what you're doing here.

00:16:21.168 --> 00:16:22.920
You don't think I know?

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.255
Are you guys

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.967
making a crew without me?
Because I'm too old?

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.302
Did you drink whiskey without me?

00:16:29.385 --> 00:16:34.015
Come on. What fun is drinking without you?

00:16:34.265 --> 00:16:38.269
You and I are only a year apart, too.

00:16:38.352 --> 00:16:40.021
I'm just as old as you are.

00:16:40.104 --> 00:16:41.814
Have fun with your security camera.

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:43.357
Huh?

00:16:44.609 --> 00:16:46.986
Bye, Su-il.

00:16:47.737 --> 00:16:49.155
I'll call you later.

00:16:50.114 --> 00:16:51.657
Don't get sulky, okay?

00:16:55.077 --> 00:16:56.162
What do we need?

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.164
Soju and beer, four bottles each.

00:16:58.247 --> 00:17:00.207
- Four bottles of soju!
- And beer.

00:17:00.291 --> 00:17:02.960
One bottle, two...

00:17:03.502 --> 00:17:04.420
Ssamjang.

00:17:04.837 --> 00:17:07.256
Ssamjang!

00:17:07.923 --> 00:17:10.092
I need a large batch of short rib cuts.

00:17:11.135 --> 00:17:13.763
Short rib cuts?

00:17:14.722 --> 00:17:17.183
- Would two of these be good?
- Yes.

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:18.684
I'd also like two packs of pork belly.

00:17:18.768 --> 00:17:19.935
Pork belly?

00:17:30.863 --> 00:17:32.073
Where's Dad?

00:17:32.156 --> 00:17:33.616
- Did we get everything?
- Yeah.

00:17:34.325 --> 00:17:35.701
- Let's go now.
- Okay.

00:17:36.327 --> 00:17:37.453
All right.

00:17:39.121 --> 00:17:40.164
- Here you go.
- Yes.

00:17:40.414 --> 00:17:42.124
- Thank you.
- Have a good day.

00:17:42.208 --> 00:17:43.334
- Goodbye!
- Have a good party.

00:17:43.417 --> 00:17:44.877
- Goodbye, cutie!
- Bye!

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.462
- Hi, Su-il.
- See you around.

00:17:46.545 --> 00:17:47.672
Hello.

00:17:47.755 --> 00:17:49.465
- Hello.
- Hi, Do-yeon. Have a good day.

00:17:52.593 --> 00:17:55.513
You seem awfully sulky again.

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:57.431
Here. For the gas station
at the intersection.

00:17:58.516 --> 00:18:01.686
They don't even have customers
because they don't take card payments.

00:18:01.769 --> 00:18:03.688
So why are they always ordering
so much coffee?

00:18:05.564 --> 00:18:08.818
Why do you care
if they chug liters of coffee every day?

00:18:10.611 --> 00:18:12.363
You're too strict on me!

00:18:16.826 --> 00:18:22.415
You make me feel terrible
for just getting a drink with the guys.

00:18:22.665 --> 00:18:25.918
Now, Yong-hui and Byeong-nam
are having fun without me.

00:18:27.086 --> 00:18:28.587
Are they leaving you out?

00:18:29.213 --> 00:18:30.506
Of course not.

00:18:32.425 --> 00:18:35.344
It's all because
you're as scary as a tiger.

00:18:35.428 --> 00:18:37.138
Everyone's too scared to say anything.

00:18:38.764 --> 00:18:40.224
I married a tiger!

00:18:41.225 --> 00:18:43.310
Where are you going? Come here.

00:18:43.978 --> 00:18:45.104
Roar!

00:19:07.668 --> 00:19:08.669
Let's go!

00:19:09.253 --> 00:19:12.256
- Left, right, down, up!
- Right on!

00:19:14.967 --> 00:19:17.178
Special combat martial arts!

00:19:26.353 --> 00:19:27.605
Oh, wow!

00:19:34.236 --> 00:19:35.362
The best!

00:19:35.446 --> 00:19:39.617
Do-yeon, you're so good. You're the best.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:40.701
Is that all?

00:19:40.785 --> 00:19:42.953
No, come here.
Uncle will give you some money.

00:19:43.662 --> 00:19:45.456
Do-yeon, put your hands together.

00:19:46.957 --> 00:19:49.251
Fine, I'll give you two bills.

00:19:49.502 --> 00:19:50.836
Thank you.

00:19:51.462 --> 00:19:52.588
Do-yeon,

00:19:52.671 --> 00:19:54.465
what's your favorite thing in the world?

00:19:54.548 --> 00:19:56.383
Going to the amusement park with Daddy.

00:19:56.926 --> 00:19:59.345
But Daddy is always too busy.

00:19:59.428 --> 00:20:03.098
I also want to go,
but that man won't let me.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.852
Do-yeon, beg this uncle

00:20:06.936 --> 00:20:09.104
to give Daddy a day off.

00:20:10.064 --> 00:20:12.733
Please let my Dad
take me to the amusement park.

00:20:14.276 --> 00:20:17.154
Do-yeon, don't put Uncle in a pickle.

00:20:17.988 --> 00:20:20.199
She really loves amusement parks.

00:20:20.574 --> 00:20:22.076
No pressure, sir.

00:20:22.535 --> 00:20:25.830
Just give in. She wants to go.

00:20:25.996 --> 00:20:27.414
No pressure.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:33.587
Fine, take a day off
and go to the amusement park with her.

00:20:34.839 --> 00:20:36.549
You don't need to do that.

00:20:36.632 --> 00:20:37.675
Yes!

00:20:39.426 --> 00:20:40.761
Yes!

00:20:40.845 --> 00:20:43.597
Honey, go to the convenience store
and get some beer.

00:20:44.014 --> 00:20:45.099
Okay.

00:21:01.407 --> 00:21:02.867
How refreshing.

00:21:11.834 --> 00:21:14.795
The Vice Minister seems to be
looking into who was at the site.

00:21:15.796 --> 00:21:18.048
What the hell is his deal?

00:21:20.217 --> 00:21:22.720
- We don't know who's behind it yet?
- No.

00:21:24.013 --> 00:21:26.891
You know how
the first victim was a foreigner?

00:21:27.224 --> 00:21:29.977
There was something about
"a new day" or whatever online.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:32.313
Felt like it could be a cult.

00:21:32.938 --> 00:21:37.610
Why don't we just go with that
and blame a cult?

00:21:37.776 --> 00:21:40.946
You think I haven't thought of that?
That's the easiest way.

00:21:42.323 --> 00:21:45.409
But those bombs keep going off,
only in Kiyun-si.

00:21:45.492 --> 00:21:47.119
That Eun-jae keeps asking...

00:21:47.202 --> 00:21:48.662
Oh, gosh! See?

00:21:48.746 --> 00:21:49.747
NA EUN-JAE

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:52.082
Speak of the devil.

00:21:54.043 --> 00:21:55.044
Ridiculous.

00:21:59.965 --> 00:22:02.551
She's just scared the plans
for the specialized zone will be canceled.

00:22:02.801 --> 00:22:05.346
That specialized zone plan
is what led us to this.

00:22:05.429 --> 00:22:06.931
Anyway,

00:22:07.848 --> 00:22:11.018
if they find out
it was our bombs exploding in Kiyun-si,

00:22:11.518 --> 00:22:12.811
it's over for all of us.

00:22:13.562 --> 00:22:15.105
Stay on your toes.

00:22:16.106 --> 00:22:17.107
Yes, sir.

00:22:24.448 --> 00:22:27.117
The call cannot be completed.
Please leave a voice message...

00:22:27.201 --> 00:22:28.452
Why, that little...

00:22:28.535 --> 00:22:30.537
Pick up your damn phone!

00:22:39.171 --> 00:22:40.798
Drop me off up there.

00:22:41.382 --> 00:22:42.383
Yes, ma'am.

00:22:42.591 --> 00:22:47.471
MAMMOSEU MART

00:22:51.183 --> 00:22:52.226
Welcome...

00:22:54.269 --> 00:22:55.229
Hey.

00:22:55.771 --> 00:22:57.481
That's not a way to greet your customer.

00:22:57.731 --> 00:22:59.984
You're not a customer
if you don't buy anything.

00:23:09.284 --> 00:23:10.619
How much is this?

00:23:12.705 --> 00:23:14.665
Keep the change.

00:23:15.249 --> 00:23:16.542
Let me ask you something.

00:23:16.625 --> 00:23:18.168
You've only visited
during election periods

00:23:18.252 --> 00:23:21.296
since graduating from high school.
What brings you here?

00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:23.340
You know how busy I am.

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:24.842
Since you're one of the leaders,

00:23:25.342 --> 00:23:27.261
you hear everything
in this neighborhood, right?

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:33.017
Did anyone record a video
of the ATM booth explosion?

00:23:33.976 --> 00:23:36.645
What if they did?
What are you trying to pull now?

00:23:36.729 --> 00:23:38.439
Pull what? You're unbelievable.

00:23:38.856 --> 00:23:40.941
I'm a congresswoman of our nation.

00:23:41.275 --> 00:23:44.403
You saw me install

00:23:44.486 --> 00:23:47.197
those smart security cameras
for this town's safety.

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:49.867
What are the ladies of the town saying?

00:23:51.410 --> 00:23:55.080
They won't vote for you in the next term
because you took too long.

00:23:58.083 --> 00:23:59.168
Eun-jae,

00:24:01.378 --> 00:24:03.172
people don't like to go near you, do they?

00:24:03.505 --> 00:24:05.591
- What?
- You can take this.

00:24:07.259 --> 00:24:08.427
Chew it up.

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:11.513
Sure, I'll chew the damn thing.

00:24:20.522 --> 00:24:22.524
- Here it comes.
- It's here.

00:24:22.608 --> 00:24:24.318
- Gosh.
- Over here!

00:24:24.401 --> 00:24:25.569
It's too early.

00:24:25.652 --> 00:24:27.905
- Come on!
- Don't say that!

00:24:28.781 --> 00:24:30.574
Thank you for coming, sir.

00:24:30.657 --> 00:24:33.702
Move more often
so we can enjoy your wife's cooking again.

00:24:33.786 --> 00:24:35.162
What are you saying? Just get in.

00:24:35.245 --> 00:24:36.121
- Bye.
- Round Two?

00:24:36.205 --> 00:24:37.915
- Come on!
- Go home!

00:24:37.998 --> 00:24:40.125
- Get home safely.
- Goodnight!

00:24:40.459 --> 00:24:41.502
- You can go, too.
- Let's go.

00:24:41.585 --> 00:24:43.587
- Thanks for the feast.
- Let's grab a drink.

00:24:43.921 --> 00:24:45.756
- My goodness!
- Come on, then.

00:24:45.839 --> 00:24:47.382
- Let's have another round.
- Go home.

00:24:47.466 --> 00:24:48.592
No, I'm fine.

00:24:48.675 --> 00:24:50.803
- No!
- Please!

00:24:50.886 --> 00:24:52.971
Let's grab another drink.
Use the company card.

00:25:15.702 --> 00:25:17.287
Gosh, I'm tired.

00:25:21.500 --> 00:25:22.459
Who are you?

00:25:43.272 --> 00:25:44.231
You up?

00:25:45.482 --> 00:25:48.110
Place your hands on the wheel, palms down.

00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:53.866
Okay.

00:25:59.413 --> 00:26:02.166
I had to wait
because I couldn't unlock your phone.

00:26:05.752 --> 00:26:06.753
There we go.

00:26:10.174 --> 00:26:12.217
If this falls off, you're dead.

00:26:12.968 --> 00:26:14.219
I'm not kidding.

00:26:19.433 --> 00:26:20.350
What?

00:26:20.851 --> 00:26:21.852
It's me.

00:26:22.853 --> 00:26:23.812
Is he with you?

00:26:24.104 --> 00:26:25.856
Yes, but...

00:26:28.525 --> 00:26:29.985
He got me.

00:26:30.861 --> 00:26:31.820
Choi Kang?

00:26:33.197 --> 00:26:35.824
Don't be stupid.
Just take the package I sent.

00:26:37.117 --> 00:26:37.951
The glove compartment.

00:26:47.502 --> 00:26:49.671
Take the phone and let the man go.

00:26:51.173 --> 00:26:53.592
Are you the one who pulled off
that "new day" bullshit?

00:26:54.384 --> 00:26:55.427
Who are you?

00:26:55.802 --> 00:26:57.179
How did you know I lived here?

00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:02.809
Why isn't he answering?

00:27:03.769 --> 00:27:05.437
It got disconnected.

00:27:05.646 --> 00:27:06.605
What?

00:27:11.902 --> 00:27:14.655
I told you you'd die if this fell off.

00:27:16.531 --> 00:27:17.950
But you took it.

00:27:21.036 --> 00:27:25.457
HARDWARE DREAM TREE STATIONERY

00:27:27.709 --> 00:27:31.046
Should I say I received or stole it?

00:27:31.338 --> 00:27:34.091
It either looks like a burner phone
or an encrypted one.

00:27:34.174 --> 00:27:35.259
It's an encrypted phone.

00:27:35.759 --> 00:27:37.678
- How do you know?
- I can tell by looking at it.

00:27:38.262 --> 00:27:39.513
Good for you, JDD.

00:27:40.389 --> 00:27:44.017
Aren't these only used in the military?

00:27:44.726 --> 00:27:47.854
He knows my name and where I live.

00:27:48.855 --> 00:27:50.691
Could it be those guys?

00:27:51.441 --> 00:27:54.778
Are they trying to contact you with this
because we blocked the satellite signals?

00:27:56.822 --> 00:27:59.533
He didn't seem to be on the same side
as the satellite laptop guys.

00:27:59.616 --> 00:28:00.575
Not those guys?

00:28:01.702 --> 00:28:02.703
The military?

00:28:03.662 --> 00:28:04.746
Not sure.

00:28:08.083 --> 00:28:09.710
How's Mr. Lee doing with the laptop?

00:28:10.168 --> 00:28:12.504
He's having a blast.

00:28:12.587 --> 00:28:13.839
Money really is good, huh?

00:28:48.874 --> 00:28:50.000
Okay.

00:28:54.046 --> 00:28:56.798
VEOTIGO INSURANCE

00:28:59.051 --> 00:29:01.553
Your subordinates
are working hard outside,

00:29:01.636 --> 00:29:04.097
and here you are,
sitting cozy in the office.

00:29:04.181 --> 00:29:06.266
Are you picking a fight?
You want a piece of this?

00:29:06.641 --> 00:29:11.104
No, I feel bad for you,
working at the office all by yourself.

00:29:11.355 --> 00:29:14.358
You didn't let me finish.
Why are you so irritated? Menopause?

00:29:15.275 --> 00:29:16.568
I should have just ignored you.

00:29:16.651 --> 00:29:19.279
I know! You've worked with me
for long enough.

00:29:19.363 --> 00:29:22.032
There's no need to respond to everything.

00:29:22.407 --> 00:29:24.701
I sent the insurance payout
for Ms. Lee Seo-hui today.

00:29:24.785 --> 00:29:25.869
Really?

00:29:27.245 --> 00:29:28.622
Thank you, sir!

00:29:29.206 --> 00:29:31.375
Did you receive
the insurance payout, Ms. Lee?

00:29:33.418 --> 00:29:34.878
I'm glad it all worked out.

00:29:35.754 --> 00:29:39.341
Did you also receive compensation
for the house damage?

00:29:41.843 --> 00:29:42.969
I see.

00:29:43.095 --> 00:29:45.222
No, they'll send the money soon.

00:29:46.139 --> 00:29:46.973
Okay.

00:29:47.766 --> 00:29:49.142
Please take care of yourself.

00:29:49.851 --> 00:29:51.603
Okay, bye.

00:29:59.569 --> 00:30:02.489
GODFATHER
LOANS WITHOUT COLLATERAL OR GUARANTEE

00:30:02.739 --> 00:30:05.200
LOAN AVAILABLE IMMEDIATELY

00:30:11.832 --> 00:30:12.666
Shoulder...

00:30:12.749 --> 00:30:14.751
INSURANCE BASTARD

00:30:15.210 --> 00:30:16.670
This little shit.

00:30:22.008 --> 00:30:24.094
It's him again. Seriously...

00:30:25.429 --> 00:30:26.638
I'll take the call.

00:30:26.721 --> 00:30:28.223
Sure.

00:30:33.645 --> 00:30:34.604
What?

00:30:34.855 --> 00:30:36.398
Hey, Godfather.

00:30:36.481 --> 00:30:39.192
You can't be a loanshark
and not pay on time.

00:30:39.568 --> 00:30:40.777
Who do you think you're calling?

00:30:41.403 --> 00:30:45.407
Aren't you the guy who smashed the table?
Was your name Sang-ho? Seong-ho?

00:30:45.490 --> 00:30:48.577
You want me to cut your stomach open?

00:30:48.660 --> 00:30:50.412
You think our boss is your buddy?

00:30:50.787 --> 00:30:53.081
Oh, you're his little brother.

00:30:53.331 --> 00:30:55.333
I didn't know it was a family business.

00:30:56.293 --> 00:30:58.795
Tell your big brother
that his payment is overdue.

00:30:58.879 --> 00:31:00.255
Where are you?

00:31:00.338 --> 00:31:01.465
In your heart.

00:31:02.048 --> 00:31:02.883
Hello?

00:31:04.384 --> 00:31:06.887
The bastard just hung up
after saying whatever he wanted.

00:31:07.220 --> 00:31:09.764
He's crazy.

00:31:17.647 --> 00:31:20.192
Hey, dipshit,
are you asking me to kill you?

00:31:20.275 --> 00:31:22.694
I mean, who actually wants to die?

00:31:22.777 --> 00:31:25.280
And you'll need to find me first
if you want to kill me.

00:31:26.031 --> 00:31:29.326
You brave little shit,
you don't think I can find you?

00:31:29.618 --> 00:31:30.535
No.

00:31:31.203 --> 00:31:32.120
Hello?

00:31:34.956 --> 00:31:37.417
Would you look at this bastard?

00:31:49.221 --> 00:31:50.430
What now?

00:31:50.555 --> 00:31:51.848
Hello, Mr. Choi.

00:31:53.141 --> 00:31:56.728
The father of Choi Do-yeon
from Kiyun Dream Kindergarten.

00:31:57.437 --> 00:32:00.941
Or shall I call you
Ms. Hwang Mi-gyeong's husband?

00:32:02.317 --> 00:32:03.360
Where are you?

00:32:03.818 --> 00:32:07.030
I'm a master at finding people,
you piece of shit.

00:32:09.533 --> 00:32:10.784
So, where are you?

00:32:11.243 --> 00:32:12.953
You're scared, aren't you?

00:32:13.537 --> 00:32:15.121
Our address is on our business card.

00:32:15.205 --> 00:32:18.041
You moron! Why would you tell him that?

00:32:32.973 --> 00:32:34.849
GODFATHER
LOANS WITHOUT COLLATERAL OR GUARANTEE

00:32:35.433 --> 00:32:37.310
GODFATHER
LOANS WITHOUT COLLATERAL OR GUARANTEE

00:32:39.396 --> 00:32:43.149
FIVE-MINUTE LOAN
WITHOUT COLLATERAL OR GUARANTEE

00:32:48.822 --> 00:32:50.115
He's actually here.

00:32:53.910 --> 00:32:55.412
You're really here.

00:33:02.335 --> 00:33:03.587
Just don't kill them.

00:33:04.504 --> 00:33:06.089
Don't kill them.

00:33:06.172 --> 00:33:08.425
What are you blabbering to yourself?

00:33:11.678 --> 00:33:16.349
All right, I'll save one limb each
for every question you answer.

00:33:16.558 --> 00:33:19.227
Or I'll break as many limbs
as the number of questions I ask.

00:33:19.686 --> 00:33:21.438
Hey, you high or something?

00:33:23.732 --> 00:33:24.566
One.

00:33:25.817 --> 00:33:27.944
How did you find out
the names of my family?

00:33:28.028 --> 00:33:30.155
From your mom. Got a problem?

00:33:30.447 --> 00:33:31.823
It's a business secret.

00:33:33.742 --> 00:33:34.701
Two.

00:33:35.035 --> 00:33:38.246
Did you ever get near the kindergarten?

00:33:38.580 --> 00:33:39.581
What if we did?

00:33:39.998 --> 00:33:43.043
Don't answer him. Just beat him up.

00:33:55.472 --> 00:33:56.306
Stop him!

00:34:09.819 --> 00:34:10.695
Damn it!

00:34:19.621 --> 00:34:20.914
No killing.

00:34:22.248 --> 00:34:23.416
No killing.

00:34:33.218 --> 00:34:34.135
Shit!

00:34:46.064 --> 00:34:47.816
I did it!

00:34:55.657 --> 00:34:56.658
Stop!

00:34:57.075 --> 00:34:58.326
Please stop!

00:34:59.744 --> 00:35:00.829
Stop it, okay?

00:35:01.663 --> 00:35:02.580
Come here.

00:35:03.957 --> 00:35:06.084
I'm sorry. It's all my fault, okay?

00:35:06.584 --> 00:35:07.836
You were behind it, weren't you?

00:35:08.211 --> 00:35:11.715
I'm sorry!
I swear, I'll stay out of your hair.

00:35:11.798 --> 00:35:13.591
I won't ever bother you again.

00:35:13.925 --> 00:35:16.219
No, wrong answer.

00:35:16.594 --> 00:35:17.637
Please...

00:35:20.181 --> 00:35:22.142
You can't open it without a key...

00:35:55.550 --> 00:35:56.634
What now?

00:35:57.343 --> 00:35:58.720
Forensic analysis is done!

00:35:58.803 --> 00:36:02.056
Everyone, to the ardware store.
No, hardware.

00:36:16.154 --> 00:36:19.699
HARDWARE DREAM TREE STATIONERY

00:36:20.492 --> 00:36:21.576
- Hello.
- Hey.

00:36:22.202 --> 00:36:23.203
Hello.

00:36:30.210 --> 00:36:32.295
There they go again.

00:36:32.670 --> 00:36:35.173
They've left me out again. Just me.

00:36:56.236 --> 00:37:00.949
I recovered the map
and the dashcam footage.

00:37:03.535 --> 00:37:05.370
Good work. You're amazing.

00:37:06.371 --> 00:37:08.122
The tools really helped.

00:37:08.206 --> 00:37:09.582
That was totally worth the money.

00:37:10.500 --> 00:37:12.502
Hey, give me some credit, too.

00:37:12.836 --> 00:37:16.506
I built this radio-wave-blocking tent
by hand.

00:37:16.589 --> 00:37:19.801
It was supposed only to block radio waves,

00:37:19.884 --> 00:37:22.762
but it almost blocked my life out, too!
I nearly died from the heat.

00:37:25.598 --> 00:37:26.975
Still got the job done, though.

00:37:27.058 --> 00:37:28.142
That's true.

00:37:28.226 --> 00:37:30.645
It costs about 30,000,000 won
to build the real thing.

00:37:30.728 --> 00:37:33.356
But I didn't even use
one-hundredth of that.

00:37:33.439 --> 00:37:35.149
- Good work.
- Thank you.

00:37:35.441 --> 00:37:37.443
I'll check the footage
and upload it right away.

00:37:37.527 --> 00:37:38.736
- Okay.
- All right.

00:37:38.820 --> 00:37:40.905
Mr. Lee, could I have a copy
of the dashcam footage?

00:37:42.532 --> 00:37:43.616
Here you go.

00:37:44.868 --> 00:37:46.286
And just call me Yong-hui.

00:37:46.911 --> 00:37:48.371
Is that all right, Yong-hui?

00:37:48.454 --> 00:37:49.497
Yes!

00:37:49.581 --> 00:37:52.458
Anyway, great work.

00:38:07.724 --> 00:38:10.518
Did you end up arguing with Byeong-nam?

00:38:10.602 --> 00:38:14.105
No, why would I argue with him?
That's a waste of time.

00:38:15.523 --> 00:38:16.524
You did, huh?

00:38:18.610 --> 00:38:20.778
Honey, the thing is,

00:38:21.529 --> 00:38:25.992
I just saw Min-seo's tutor,
Producer Kim of Magnifying Media, and Kang

00:38:26.075 --> 00:38:28.578
all gathering at the hardware store.

00:38:28.661 --> 00:38:29.621
Without me.

00:38:29.996 --> 00:38:31.623
So? Join them.

00:38:32.081 --> 00:38:34.542
Me? I can't.

00:38:34.626 --> 00:38:36.544
How could I go when I wasn't invited?

00:38:37.086 --> 00:38:38.922
How could I join them? I can't.

00:38:40.298 --> 00:38:45.053
Even Chun-bae hasn't seen Byeong-nam
since Myeong-o's funeral.

00:38:47.180 --> 00:38:49.807
The Byeong-nam we knew of is gone.
He's changed.

00:38:50.266 --> 00:38:51.267
And I'm alone.

00:38:51.893 --> 00:38:52.936
It's fine.

00:38:53.019 --> 00:38:55.521
I'll just clean that up.
Who am I to be sad?

00:39:00.276 --> 00:39:02.695
What are they scheming?

00:39:04.864 --> 00:39:08.284
- Good work.
- Yong-hui, you're awesome.

00:39:08.368 --> 00:39:09.494
It's nothing.

00:39:09.577 --> 00:39:11.287
- Good work.
- It was impressive.

00:39:11.371 --> 00:39:12.497
Oh, hello.

00:39:22.799 --> 00:39:25.259
I'll get going first.
I have some editing to do.

00:39:25.343 --> 00:39:26.678
Please excuse me.

00:39:27.428 --> 00:39:28.930
I'd better get going, too.

00:39:29.597 --> 00:39:30.556
Me too.

00:39:31.099 --> 00:39:32.141
Hello, ma'am.

00:39:33.142 --> 00:39:35.269
I need a shower.

00:39:35.353 --> 00:39:36.437
Bye.

00:39:39.941 --> 00:39:42.694
I also need to tidy up the stationery...

00:39:46.739 --> 00:39:47.657
Byeong-nam.

00:39:49.158 --> 00:39:50.910
What now?

00:39:52.245 --> 00:39:54.372
What are you guys plotting?

00:40:03.006 --> 00:40:06.134
HARDWARE DREAM TREE STATIONERY

00:40:09.512 --> 00:40:12.432
She's been in there for over 20 minutes.
What's taking her so long?

00:40:14.475 --> 00:40:15.435
Man...

00:40:16.269 --> 00:40:19.397
It must be really tough
for my poor Byeong-nam.

00:40:21.399 --> 00:40:23.443
It's okay. I live with that every day.

00:40:27.071 --> 00:40:30.074
It was just too odd, okay?

00:40:30.283 --> 00:40:32.702
Explosions kept going off
in the neighborhood.

00:40:32.910 --> 00:40:35.288
Kang and I just so happened
to witness one of them,

00:40:35.371 --> 00:40:39.000
so we teamed up
to get to the bottom of it.

00:40:39.083 --> 00:40:40.877
That's all.

00:40:41.878 --> 00:40:43.212
You traitor.

00:40:44.922 --> 00:40:47.842
So you're family
only when you're out drinking at night?

00:40:48.342 --> 00:40:51.637
All these things are happening,
and you guys are keeping it from us?

00:40:51.763 --> 00:40:54.140
What's the point of scaring everyone
with all of this?

00:40:54.223 --> 00:40:57.268
Am I telling you to tell everyone in town?

00:40:57.393 --> 00:40:59.312
You should've at least told
Chun-bae and me!

00:40:59.395 --> 00:41:01.355
We're also leaders of the neighborhood.

00:41:01.439 --> 00:41:04.901
Chun-bae is too busy
with his wife right now,

00:41:04.984 --> 00:41:06.527
and you're...

00:41:07.070 --> 00:41:08.154
What?

00:41:11.574 --> 00:41:15.369
My naive little husband
thought you were pretending to be busy

00:41:15.453 --> 00:41:17.497
to hang out with Yong-hui
and Kang without him.

00:41:17.580 --> 00:41:18.873
He's pouting like crazy.

00:41:19.707 --> 00:41:21.125
That's not all.

00:41:21.542 --> 00:41:24.253
He thinks you guys don't come to the store
because you're scared of me.

00:41:24.837 --> 00:41:26.130
That's not entirely wrong.

00:41:27.757 --> 00:41:28.841
Damn it.

00:41:29.300 --> 00:41:30.676
Come on!

00:41:31.219 --> 00:41:34.388
If Su-il knew about this,
he would've told the whole town!

00:41:36.599 --> 00:41:40.645
He's friendly, yes.
But he can keep a secret better than you.

00:41:44.732 --> 00:41:46.692
I don't care
about what you guys are doing.

00:41:47.276 --> 00:41:50.196
Just don't leave my husband out. Got that?

00:41:52.782 --> 00:41:56.160
Get to the bottom of it...
What can you even do?

00:42:25.022 --> 00:42:28.985
Honey, my boss gave me a day off
to go to the amusement park.

00:42:29.277 --> 00:42:31.779
Really? That's great.

00:42:32.405 --> 00:42:33.865
Do-yeon will be so happy.

00:42:34.907 --> 00:42:37.076
But do we have to go?

00:42:37.160 --> 00:42:40.079
With all that news
about park rides malfunctioning.

00:42:41.080 --> 00:42:43.875
How do you give her baths?
Aren't you scared she'll drown, too?

00:42:44.458 --> 00:42:46.836
You're so overprotective of her.

00:42:47.670 --> 00:42:50.214
All of Do-yeon's friends
have been to amusement parks.

00:42:50.298 --> 00:42:51.507
All except Do-yeon.

00:42:53.050 --> 00:42:55.428
Still, we don't need to go now--

00:42:55.511 --> 00:42:58.472
We do. You got a day off.

00:42:58.931 --> 00:43:01.142
Cut the crap. We're taking her.

00:43:02.101 --> 00:43:03.352
- Lights out.
- Yes, ma'am.

00:43:22.163 --> 00:43:23.539
The video will be up at midnight.

00:43:23.915 --> 00:43:25.333
Please like, comment, and subscribe.

00:43:28.544 --> 00:43:31.756
Here's the dashcam footage
we were able to track down.

00:43:33.716 --> 00:43:36.844
On the laptop of the foreigner
who died in the ATM explosion

00:43:37.220 --> 00:43:39.472
was a video of the crash
at the Kiyun Intersection,

00:43:39.555 --> 00:43:41.307
along with a suspicious map.

00:43:41.724 --> 00:43:46.479
What's scarier is that there was a message
foreshadowing a terrorist attack.

00:43:46.729 --> 00:43:49.690
Despite the government's announcement
that the three explosions were accidental,

00:43:50.274 --> 00:43:54.528
we've found evidence
that these explosions were planned.

00:43:54.612 --> 00:43:57.949
In the next video,
we'll reveal the organizations and people

00:43:58.032 --> 00:44:02.578
associated with the explosions,
based on our research.

00:44:03.412 --> 00:44:04.413
Thank you.

00:44:04.497 --> 00:44:05.748
WHAT'S HAPPENING TO OUR CITY?

00:44:05.831 --> 00:44:07.375
A NEW DAY IS COMING

00:44:52.461 --> 00:44:54.005
Welcome!

00:44:56.340 --> 00:44:58.676
It'd be good to avoid crowds
as much as we can.

00:44:58.759 --> 00:44:59.760
Whatever.

00:45:00.011 --> 00:45:03.180
You sound like an old man.
Just let Do-yeon have a blast, okay?

00:45:03.597 --> 00:45:06.559
It's been her dream
to come here with her dad.

00:45:06.642 --> 00:45:07.852
She's living her dream today.

00:45:08.561 --> 00:45:10.104
Oh, a bunny!

00:45:12.440 --> 00:45:14.608
Daddy, come on!

00:45:15.359 --> 00:45:18.612
- Don't run, Do-yeon! You'll trip!
- She'll be fine.

00:45:18.946 --> 00:45:21.866
She's very athletic
because she takes after me.

00:45:21.949 --> 00:45:23.743
I hope she takes after me
for everything else.

00:45:25.328 --> 00:45:26.912
Daddy is coming to get you!

00:45:33.127 --> 00:45:37.506
How cute. My eldest son
is playing with my daughter.

00:45:39.008 --> 00:45:40.426
I'm coming, too!

00:45:40.509 --> 00:45:42.053
Here she comes!

00:46:12.291 --> 00:46:13.125
Do-yeon!

00:46:56.502 --> 00:47:00.172
#KIYUN-SI, #BOMBING,
#TERRORIST THREAT, #A NEW DAY IS COMING

00:47:06.595 --> 00:47:09.473
NATIONAL THREAT RESPONSE CENTER

00:47:10.391 --> 00:47:11.559
Yes, this is the situation room.

00:47:12.935 --> 00:47:14.562
A bomb threat in Kiyun-si?

00:47:14.895 --> 00:47:18.149
- So you're saying that...
- This is the situation room.

00:47:22.278 --> 00:47:24.155
What? A bomb threat?

00:47:27.616 --> 00:47:29.952
On social media?

00:47:30.035 --> 00:47:31.036
Attention, everyone!

00:47:31.829 --> 00:47:34.165
Get all security camera footage
from Kiyun-si on the screen

00:47:34.248 --> 00:47:35.791
and look for any odd signs.

00:47:38.544 --> 00:47:39.962
KIYUN MIDDLE SCHOOL

00:47:40.045 --> 00:47:41.172
What do you want to do tomorrow?

00:47:42.047 --> 00:47:43.215
Eat something good?

00:47:43.382 --> 00:47:44.383
Sure.

00:47:44.925 --> 00:47:46.552
- Bye!
- Bye!

00:47:58.522 --> 00:48:00.566
Sir, look at this!

00:48:01.692 --> 00:48:02.526
What is it?

00:48:03.194 --> 00:48:04.361
Look over here.

00:48:19.752 --> 00:48:21.921
You have tutoring today, right?
Don't be late.

00:48:23.005 --> 00:48:24.673
Yeah, I'm waiting for the bus now.

00:48:27.468 --> 00:48:29.428
Did you go over the material?

00:48:30.179 --> 00:48:32.389
Come on, stop nagging me.

00:48:37.811 --> 00:48:38.812
Whose bag is that?

00:48:39.605 --> 00:48:40.856
I should put it on the bench.

00:48:51.825 --> 00:48:55.204
MAMMOSEU MART

00:49:02.044 --> 00:49:03.045
Min-seo!

00:49:04.171 --> 00:49:05.548
Min-seo!

00:49:16.600 --> 00:49:18.269
You can't come in, it's dangerous.
Stay back.

00:49:18.519 --> 00:49:19.937
- Let me through.
- It's dangerous. Please step back.

00:49:20.020 --> 00:49:21.146
- Let me through.
- Please step back.

00:49:21.230 --> 00:49:22.231
Let me through!

00:49:26.110 --> 00:49:26.986
Chief?

00:49:28.404 --> 00:49:29.738
Let me through. I'm going in.

00:49:29.822 --> 00:49:32.324
No, the EOD team is on the way.
What's going on?

00:49:33.534 --> 00:49:34.577
It's my daughter in there.

00:49:42.960 --> 00:49:44.086
No, please!

00:49:45.254 --> 00:49:46.255
Min-seo!

00:50:08.652 --> 00:50:09.945
Mom...

00:50:11.989 --> 00:50:13.699
Mom...

00:50:14.366 --> 00:50:15.326
Min-seo,

00:50:17.828 --> 00:50:18.912
it'll be over in no time.

00:50:19.830 --> 00:50:20.664
You trust me, right?

00:50:22.583 --> 00:50:23.542
Yes.

00:50:29.381 --> 00:50:30.341
Good girl.

00:50:31.842 --> 00:50:32.760
It's okay.

00:50:34.303 --> 00:50:35.638
It'll be fine. Slowly.

00:50:37.973 --> 00:50:39.099
I got you.

00:50:44.313 --> 00:50:45.606
Let me take a look.

00:51:01.955 --> 00:51:02.873
Min-seo.

00:51:03.582 --> 00:51:04.958
Min-seo.

00:51:05.042 --> 00:51:06.919
Look at me.

00:51:07.711 --> 00:51:08.921
We have more than enough time.

00:51:10.422 --> 00:51:13.801
Min-seo, I can do it, okay?

00:51:15.302 --> 00:51:16.303
It'll be okay.

00:52:51.607 --> 00:52:52.733
It's all over.

00:52:54.568 --> 00:52:55.819
It's all good now.

00:52:57.863 --> 00:52:59.156
Good job, Min-seo.

00:53:01.200 --> 00:53:02.367
It's all over.

00:53:05.954 --> 00:53:07.372
Good job, Min-seo.

00:53:09.208 --> 00:53:11.585
Min-seo. I'm here, sweetie.

00:53:13.337 --> 00:53:17.424
I'm so proud of you.

00:53:17.508 --> 00:53:20.469
Good job, Min-seo.

00:53:25.224 --> 00:53:27.476
You were amazing.

00:53:39.321 --> 00:53:43.659
This afternoon, a suspicious backpack
possibly containing a bomb was reported.

00:53:43.742 --> 00:53:46.161
The police and military
responded immediately.

00:53:46.495 --> 00:53:49.289
The bomb in question
was revealed to be a fake,

00:53:49.373 --> 00:53:51.959
with no explosive risk.

00:53:52.042 --> 00:53:54.837
The conspiracies and fake news
are getting out of control.

00:53:54.920 --> 00:53:57.923
Look at it now.
Even kids are pulling terrorist pranks.

00:53:59.758 --> 00:54:00.968
Hey!

00:54:01.051 --> 00:54:03.554
Are you fucking kidding me?

00:54:04.513 --> 00:54:08.058
They're all anti-state forces!

00:54:08.517 --> 00:54:10.477
Arrest them right now
and interrogate them.

00:54:12.229 --> 00:54:15.148
MAGNIFYING MEDIA

00:54:28.120 --> 00:54:30.873
What? What the hell?

00:54:31.331 --> 00:54:32.666
Hey! What's going on?

00:54:32.749 --> 00:54:34.126
Hold on!

00:54:34.209 --> 00:54:36.420
Hey, don't touch the server!

00:54:37.588 --> 00:54:39.339
What's going on?

00:54:39.673 --> 00:54:41.091
Who the hell are you?

00:54:42.301 --> 00:54:44.094
Hey, where...

00:54:45.554 --> 00:54:47.014
Where are you taking me?

00:54:47.973 --> 00:54:49.099
What is this?

00:54:49.433 --> 00:54:50.934
Damn it!

00:55:09.328 --> 00:55:10.913
I want ice cream.

00:55:10.996 --> 00:55:12.247
You had some earlier.

00:55:12.539 --> 00:55:14.291
Can I have one more?

00:55:14.416 --> 00:55:16.627
No, too much cold food
will upset your stomach.

00:55:20.088 --> 00:55:21.381
My stomach is fine.

00:55:21.465 --> 00:55:23.258
I want another one, too.

00:55:26.136 --> 00:55:29.306
Mommy, just one more, please?

00:55:29.556 --> 00:55:30.849
I promise not to upset my stomach.

00:55:31.558 --> 00:55:33.268
She says she won't upset her stomach.

00:55:33.352 --> 00:55:35.354
- Mom.
- Mom.

00:55:35.437 --> 00:55:38.273
- Mom.
- Mom.

00:55:38.357 --> 00:55:39.566
Stop it.

00:55:39.650 --> 00:55:41.401
It's on you if Do-yeon gets a stomachache.

00:55:41.485 --> 00:55:43.403
Yes! I'll take care of you
if you get a stomachache!

00:55:43.487 --> 00:55:44.488
Okay!

00:55:44.821 --> 00:55:47.866
The line for ice cream is long,
so I'll get it for us.

00:55:47.950 --> 00:55:49.743
Okay, I'll go to the bathroom
with Do-yeon.

00:55:49.826 --> 00:55:51.286
- Okay, I'll meet you there.
- Okay.

00:55:51.370 --> 00:55:52.454
I want strawberry ice cream!

00:55:52.537 --> 00:55:53.747
Okay, strawberry it is!

00:56:08.220 --> 00:56:09.221
All right.

00:56:09.972 --> 00:56:12.683
Do-yeon, I also need to use the bathroom.

00:56:12.766 --> 00:56:14.685
- So don't go anywhere and wait, okay?
- Okay.

00:56:15.227 --> 00:56:16.853
Here.

00:56:26.738 --> 00:56:28.490
Hi, could we use the sink?

00:57:22.919 --> 00:57:25.547
Do-yeon! Where did you get that ice cream?

00:57:26.715 --> 00:57:28.383
He said it was from you.

00:57:31.511 --> 00:57:32.512
Who?

00:57:36.808 --> 00:57:38.685
Some guy.

00:57:39.936 --> 00:57:42.147
It's fine. You can eat it. It's melting.

00:59:26.501 --> 00:59:29.421
HEROES NEXT DOOR

00:59:32.841 --> 00:59:35.010
- Good shot!
- Good shot!

00:59:35.093 --> 00:59:37.512
- Did it swerve? Where did it go?
- It went straight.

00:59:37.929 --> 00:59:39.723
- As straight as an arrow.
- As long as I made it.

00:59:42.434 --> 00:59:43.351
Hey.

00:59:43.935 --> 00:59:45.478
Yes, Kim Seok-jun speaking.

00:59:48.815 --> 00:59:50.025
Come on.

00:59:51.193 --> 00:59:55.197
If you start complicating things,
it won't end, you know?

00:59:55.447 --> 00:59:59.159
Imagine what a mess it'll be
if we let anti-state forces run wild.

01:00:00.744 --> 01:00:02.454
Terrorism isn't just about bombs.

01:00:03.455 --> 01:00:07.042
Spreading false news to our people
is also terrorism.

01:00:07.125 --> 01:00:11.004
I'll take care of it, all right?
I'll send in someone good.

01:00:11.087 --> 01:00:13.715
Don't worry about it.

01:00:15.091 --> 01:00:17.052
Yeah, exactly.

01:00:18.011 --> 01:00:20.722
Let's grab a meal sometime. Okay.

01:00:21.848 --> 01:00:22.849
Bye.

01:00:24.434 --> 01:00:26.978
This thick-headed moron.

01:00:27.312 --> 01:00:29.272
- Let's get moving.
- Okay.

01:00:31.399 --> 01:00:34.236
Why can't he just take a hint?

01:00:35.487 --> 01:00:36.488
Who's this?

01:00:38.448 --> 01:00:39.449
Hello?

01:00:39.950 --> 01:00:41.284
Minister Kim.

01:00:42.953 --> 01:00:44.079
Yes, who's this?

01:00:46.623 --> 01:00:47.916
It's me,

01:00:47.999 --> 01:00:49.334
Sullivan.

01:00:52.587 --> 01:00:54.256
James Sullivan?

01:01:34.671 --> 01:01:36.840
The government could be controlling it,

01:01:36.923 --> 01:01:39.426
or they could really be moving in secret.

01:01:39.509 --> 01:01:42.762
Who are these bastards
playing with bombs in our neighborhood?

01:01:42.846 --> 01:01:46.308
She was the youngest drill instructor
of the 707th Unit?

01:01:46.391 --> 01:01:48.518
What's with all the special forces
in this neighborhood?

01:01:48.601 --> 01:01:49.519
What happened?

01:01:49.602 --> 01:01:52.355
- Minister Kim, you could get screwed.
- Screw you.

01:01:52.439 --> 01:01:55.400
Something's going on,
and Kiyun-si is at the center of it.

01:01:55.483 --> 01:01:57.193
They would have been smart.

01:01:57.527 --> 01:02:01.323
Then shouldn't we
find a way to outsmart them?

01:02:03.575 --> 01:02:05.577
Subtitle translation by Min-sun Kim